  "term": "relational learning",
  "definition": "In cognition, relational learning is learning that is not limited to the trained items but transfers to novel stimuli by responding to the relation they instantiate. In the source packet, it contrasts with item-specific learning and is the basis for inferring acquisition of abstract concepts.",
